      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T09:31:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "disconnectFromCell is actually badly named, it doesn\u0027t disconnect from cell, it just unregisters a cell network request that was previously registered. So this won\u0027t actually trigger a battery stats update.\n\nActually toggling mobile data here may work instead; I think this can be done with (untested, so needs verification):\n\n```\nfinal TelephonyManager tm \u003d mContext.getSystemService(TelephonyManager.class)\n    .createForSubscriptionId(SubscriptionManager.getDefaultDataSubscriptionId());\nrunAsShell(MODIFY_PHONE_STATE, () -\u003e tm.setDataEnabledForReason(\n                TelephonyManager.DATA_ENABLED_REASON_USER, false));\n```\n\nThen don\u0027t forget to wrap the test in a try/finally, to restore mobile data at the end of the method.",
      "revId": "04fc6c69202f1df03122c72942bf98693ec93d4a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
